  "description": {
    "en": "Switzerland's gross external debt on the IMF standard presentation: the liabilities side of the external balance sheet only. A single hierarchy encodes two classifications at once — borrowing sector (public, SNB, banks, other sectors, direct-investment loans) and maturity (short or long term), each split further into debt securities and other liabilities. Starts later than the wider investment position because the standardised template post-dates it."
  },
